# Recovery-intent stub markers.
#
# patch_recovery.regenerate_from_intent() writes .recovery-intent-<slug>.txt as a
# last-resort placeholder so a missing branch at least has a branch again. It is a
# marker, NOT work (see runner/recovery_stub_detector.py). 188 of them had
# accumulated at repo root on master, swept in by agent worktrees running
# `git add -A`, and every one of them is a permanent conflict source: any branch
# that also creates a marker collides on repo root, which is exactly how
# relfix-beethoven-299c6b3c3bc6 ended up conflicting on .gitignore plus two
# .recovery-intent-*.txt files after four redo attempts.
#
# Ignoring them stops the accidental sweep-in. patch_recovery still commits its own
# marker deliberately, via `git add -f`, so that path is unaffected.
.recovery-intent-*.txt
